WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.500
 Thank you, Dan and Deb. It's truly an honor to be here today. Before I go any

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:12.240
 further, I'd like to, in the tradition of African culture, we always ask our

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:15.000
 elders for permission to speak.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.910
 So, before I go any further, I'd like to ask Imam Shahid if I have permission

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:22.000
 to proceed. Thank you.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:30.980
 It's an honor today to announce to you one of the giants in the city of

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:35.670
 Cleveland who I've had the privilege and honor to get to know over the last few

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:40.000
 years, Elle Hodge, Amir Khaled, A. Samad.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:45.040
 The supreme is to honor him because he's always been my friend and my brother

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:50.000
 and my son. Amir Khaled is Samad's president of the Coalition for Better Life,

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.000
 and many of you know him as "Peace in the Hood."

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:58.460
 Khaled is the second African-American and first Muslim to be inducted into the

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:09.000
 Cleveland International Hall of Fame. We are the field camera rockers.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:14.360
 We call him the ubiquitous Reverend Dr. Otis Moss Jr. receiving a song. There

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:18.940
 are not many people that understand the historical context of African

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:24.580
 excellence in indigenous, authentic African-American leadership in the city of

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.000
 Cleveland and many urban centers across the United States of America.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:28.430
 In the late 1980s, Khaled was part of the formation of Coalition for Better

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:31.140
 Life with legendary transformational leaders such as Omar Ali Vaid and the

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:40.000
 Prime Minister himself, R.L. Jones.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:45.560
 Many emerging community leaders like our president mayor, the 56th Mayor of the

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:51.110
 city of Cleveland, Mayor Frank G. Jackson, joined Khaled, Omar, and Harlan and

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:56.330
 others to address socio-economic inequity and issues that cause and continue to

00:01:56.330 --> 00:02:00.000
 cause distress in poor urban and minority communities.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.780
 This movement led to the first ever gang summit here in Cleveland in the United

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:14.000
 States in 1993 and was the capitalist for the historical Mid-Yam-March in 1995.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:21.000
 He is a minister of culture, an activist, a mentor, a friend, and a family man.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:26.000
 Also here he was a heck of a basketball player back in the day.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:30.920
 Khaled is a minister of culture because he has developed Muslim groups by using

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:34.000
 a guide by several principles of the Nguza-Saba.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:40.080
 He is an activist because we are a core and oppressed people. You can count on

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:46.000
 him to encourage them not to let, in his famous words, the whisper of self-sabotage,

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:49.000
 the story of self-esteem, self-determination, and greatness.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:54.400
 He is a mentor because he has helped a countless number of men and women,

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:59.780
 including myself, some of whom society have given up on because of their

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:04.000
 involvement in gangs and penal institutions and the criminal industrial complex.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:08.860
 In their transition from, in his words, once again, "stake and think" to

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:12.000
 understand their true self and greatness.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:16.860
 He is a friend to the community, but we can always count on him when something

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:22.090
 tragic happens, rather than be the loss of innocence, a child, families who

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:24.000
 have lost a loved one,

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:29.360
 senseless violence by misguided individuals, chaotic situations when the

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:35.110
 community needs steady, respected leaders and street creators to lead us

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:39.360
 through some of the most tumultuous times our country has experienced in our

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:40.000
 city as well.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:45.720
 He always speaks truth to power, with strength and grit. But most of all, he is

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:49.000
 a family man. His friends and family are with us today.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:53.050
 Khalid is vigilant and loyal to the needs of his mother, staying true to

00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:56.000
 African culture and taking care of our elders.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:00.970
 He is a nurturer to his family members. He has four wonderful daughters who

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:04.000
 listen to this. This is one of the most impressive things.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:11.170
 There are graduates from Yale, the University of Pennsylvania, Temple and

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:13.000
 George Washington.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:22.000
 As a matter of fact, African American excellence has had its excellence.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:26.060
 I first met Khalid in the 1990s when I worked with a group of young men who

00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:28.000
 were in my rights and passes program.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:32.690
 My co-facilitator, the white secretary of the Senate, told me, "We have to

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:36.000
 invite this brother to lead the Harambee circle."

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:40.560
 I was struck by his passion, vision, focus and love for black people and all

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:42.000
 people in general.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:46.860
 After knowing him for more than 20 years, Khalid Samad still has that same

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:50.000
 passion, vision, focus and love for people.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:56.460
 Ladies and gentlemen, it is my honor to introduce Khalid Samad and in the

00:04:56.460 --> 00:05:00.320
 spirit of Harambee, which means joining together for a difficult tense, my

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:07.000
 brother in the struggle, Harambee, Harambee, Harambee, Khalid Samad.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:31.000
 [applause]

